{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/pulls/3147","id":5111049497,"node_id":"PR_kwDODboMws8AAAABMKRtGQ","html_url":"https://github.com/teststuffstash/homelab/pull/3147","diff_url":"https://github.com/teststuffstash/homelab/pull/3147.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/teststuffstash/homelab/pull/3147.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/issues/3147","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/pulls/3147/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/pulls/3147/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/issues/3147/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/teststuffstash/homelab/statuses/dd452d85dc02f12d0fbfd5c794eeec51bbe96770","number":3147,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"spike: the agent loop as five islands — §C8 re-measure + snippets-v0.6.9 specs per island (DRAFT, second jail)","user":{"login":"RasmusSoot","id":1532090,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzIwOTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1532090?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RasmusSoot","html_url":"https://github.com/RasmusSoot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RasmusSoot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RasmusSoot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RasmusSoot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RasmusSoot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RasmusSoot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RasmusSoot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RasmusSoot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RasmusSoot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RasmusSoot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**DRAFT from the second jail.** Findings only, nothing decided. Started 2026-11-01 as the §C8 re-measure; on 2026-11-07 the operator ordered an unattended night run to write up the five pieces as islands.\n\n## What it records\n- **§C8**: the agent loop re-measured on October commits (unchanged from the first push).\n- **`agents/islands/{scan,launch,review,intake,retro}/`**: each island gets a README (membership, consumer contracts, read set, revert class) and a `specs/` root in the **allure-behavior-snippets v0.6.9** shape. That means contract pages with sibling `*.schema.json` files (`x-requirements`), decision tables, a glossary, worlds, and a UC-1 walk-through with committed data. The specs describe the *redrawn* contracts: the launch, review and retro rides admit through gateway `POST /sessions`, and the GitHub grammar uses ADR-122's single machine block. Every remaining old-contract site (`/route`, `/router-status`, `resolve-model.sh`, model literals) is a `⚑ gap` row with counts from the code.\n\n  | island | reqs | with a replay fixture | notes |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | scan | 35 | 33 | 7 pages; the updater/reflex mechanism moved out of `merge-path.md` |\n  | launch | 31 | 23 | 6 pages; `fixer-context.md` and the launcher half of `model-routing.md` moved |\n  | review | 28 | 14 (+9 self-test/smoke) | 6 pages; `specs-reviewer.md` and `spec-gate-tiering.md` moved |\n  | intake | 30 | 24 | 7 pages; UC-1 is the #3048 key rows → #3096 fixture dirs join; `remediation-would-scoreboard.md` moved |\n  | retro | 28 | 12 (+14 unittest) | 6 pages; the retro half of `observability-and-retro.md` moved (−24.7 KB) |\n- **No requirement has evidence.** Replay emits no `rule()` labels or Allure stories, so every row is `🚧 WIP — no evidence pipeline yet (fixture: …)`. No spec gate, join ratchet or specs reviewer reads these roots: the claim's `specs` field admits one root pair, and that pair is the gateway's.\n- **Doc moves** leave every old heading in place as a one-line pointer, so no inbound link breaks and no script changed. Nothing a pod reads at runtime moved: the coordinator brief, ground rules, recipes, lenses, `gateway/intake.md` and `docs/intake/*` stay where they are and are cited from the specs.\n- **§C8a** lists what the write-up found that contradicts the §C8 table: missing members, shared helpers counted as island code, seams inside manifests, the single-spec-root assumption, and the bucket-A series still being scored in prose with no code behind it.\n- **Glossary:** a new row \"island\" (this PR coins `agents/islands/`). The doc table, glossary, board-sweep and roles.md links now point at the moved docs.\n\n## Known shortcomings of the draft\n- `SCAN-CLAUSE-FLEET` and `SCAN-SIGNAL-REVERT` have no schema annotation, so a rule-7 gate would flag them as orphans.\n- The `> **External:**` lines (GitHub REST, Argo) were not read this session and are marked \"verify during implementation\".\n\n## Loose ends for the primary to route (no FU minted — second jail)\n1. The claim's `specs` becomes a list, together with `evidence_bucket`, the `gateway-evidence` artifact name and `build_pack`'s one `--specs-root`. Draft contract: `agents/islands/review/specs/specs-gate.md`.\n2. The replay harness needs to emit `rule()` and Allure stories, plus a join of fixture `rows` against spec tables (P4/P5). This is the first deliverable that would make these pages real.\n3. Launch: a launcher killed mid-ride sends no gateway outcome (the reaper ends the session with no strike). Gateway rides also post `AGENT_STRIKE:` and `POST /report`, so strikes double-count. The admission request hard-codes `stack: platform`. Defers exit 0 or 1, which is ambiguous. The `bound-dispatch` row sends `tier: strong`, which the gateway schema does not allow. The goal-budget gate reserves `cap_usd` on gateway rides.\n4. Launch, comment trust: the newest-review readability check reads untrusted reviews, and withheld items are dropped without a count.\n5. Review: a repo in no claim gets an empty lens map, so the migration and gate-change lenses lose their blocking line. A lockfile-only major does not select the migration lens, although the lens text and the prompt say it does.\n6. Intake: the header of `intake-select.sh` names a test that does not exist. The receipt has no `split` outcome, so a split item comes back the next day. The CronWorkflow sits only for `--island gateway`. Nothing checks that a PR ships one fixture per key row.\n7. Retro: `retro-rank.py` has no caller. `retro_queue.py` scans every issue (all states, all pages) on each acceptance and writes labels outside the shared parser. The retro templates use the `agent-coordinator` image with no tag, so a pin cannot revert them. The comment \"auto-merge NOT armed\" in the harvest template is stale. The bucket-A series needs real scoring code.\n8. Scan: `major-handoff.sh` duplicates the reflex's jq definitions. Nothing detects a scan that dispatches the wrong unit (P4 detector). The `/router-status` and `/report/latest` reads should move to the gateway.\n9. Gateway specs: the task, namespace and pod names in `uc-1/bind-request.json` differ from what the launcher actually sends. In `access.md`, a retro world says the retro is \"role-rail-denied\" on opencode, but the deployed `policy.json` grants it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-01T20:04:43Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T19:23:37Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"teststuffstash:spike/agent-loop-subcut","ref":"spike/agent-loop-subcut","repo":{"id":230296770,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkyMzAyOTY3NzA=","name":"homelab","full_name":"teststuffstash/homelab","owner":{"login":"teststuffstash","id":97731433,"node_id":"O_kgDOBdNDaQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars